eReload=true)`. [Task 7]\\n2012:- Both `/Users/oozoofrog/Movies/ReScene` and `/Volumes/eyedisk/AI/LocalAIHub` returned the same enabled `computer-use:computer-use` result under forced fresh app-server lookup. Composer queries include host/roots/cwd and have about five-minute stale/gc caching, so a project-local stale result is plausible but was not proven as the cause. [Task 7]\\n2019:- New app-server success does not refresh the running Desktop server or its Composer cache. The next acceptance check is the affected ReScene chat: Settings → Skills → refresh, then search `$computer`; without its observed result, report the UI issue as unresolved. Computer Use cannot inspect Codex itself because `Computer Use is not allowed to use the app 'com.openai.codex' for safety reasons.` [Task 7]\\n2270:- audit, skill-creator, SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, prompt-cleanup, GPT-6-Astra, progressive-disclosure, quick_validate.py, app-server, forceReload\\n2292:- Create `audit` with the local skill-creator scaffold, replace TODOs, run `quick_validate.py`, then use a fresh `codex app-server --stdio` `skills/list` with `forceReload`. Valid frontmatter and loader exposure do not prove behavior; test in-scope and out-of-scope calls when needed. [Task 2]\\n2500:- A one-shot EOF app-server stream returned only initialization; keep an interactive `codex app-server --stdio` process through `skills/list` when verifying loader exposure. Historical failures in CHANGELOG/TEST_REPORT are not active plugin registrations. [Task 2]\\n\"}}",
